course: dictionary
lesson: 14625
title: Postdate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Postdate is a verb made of two parts. Post- means after, and date is the day. So to postdate something means to put a later date on it than the day you really write it.
explain: Imagine you write a cheque on Monday but put Friday's date on it. «Mum wrote the cheque today and postdated it to Friday.» The bank cannot take the money until Friday, because the cheque only counts from that later day.
explain: Grown-ups and scientists also use postdate for things that come after other things. «These houses postdate the castle» means the houses were built after the castle. Postdate is the opposite of predate, which means to come before.
fact: Post- means after, so postdate means to put a date that comes later.
fact: «Postdate» means to write a date later than the day you write it.
fact: «A postdated cheque» cannot be cashed until the date written on it.
fact: «Postdate» can also mean to happen after something else, as in «postdate the war».
fact: «Predate» is the opposite: it means to come before something.
exercise: «Sara wrote the cheque on Monday but postdated it to Friday.» What does postdated mean here? | Written in red ink | *Given a later date, so it counts from Friday | Torn into small pieces | Paid in cash straight away
exercise: Which word is the opposite of postdate? | Postpone | Dated | Update | *Predate
exercise: «These houses postdate the castle.» What does this tell you? | The houses are the same age as the castle | The castle was built after the houses | *The houses were built after the castle | The castle is made of houses
test: «Tom's cheque is postdated to next Tuesday.» When can the bank cash it? | Never | Today | *Not before next Tuesday | Last Tuesday
test: Which sentence uses postdate to mean come after? | *«The fossils postdate the dinosaurs by many years.» | «The fossils are very shiny.» | «The fossils were sold at the fair.» | «The fossils are made of dinosaurs.»
exam: Which is true of a postdated cheque? | It must be torn up at once | *It can be cashed only from the date written on it | It can be cashed today, whatever the date | It has no date at all
